<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 2021 Diagrams and Equations for Word Problems"><h2>Warm-up — Notice and Wonder</h2><p>Consider original bar descriptions: 142 and20; four equal parts5; or142 with four additional5 parts. What does the unknown represent? The teacher reviews the publisher's diagrams.</p><h2>Activity 1 — Match situations and equations</h2><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Source cards</th><th>Original relationship</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A and F</td><td>225 + 48 − 70</td><td>203</td></tr><tr><td>C and J</td><td>225 − (6 × 10)</td><td>165</td></tr><tr><td>D and L</td><td>225 + (7 × 10)</td><td>295</td></tr><tr><td>E and G</td><td>225 + (6 × 10)</td><td>285</td></tr><tr><td>I (original diagram assignment requires teacher verification)</td><td>225 + 35 + 72</td><td>332</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Illustrative source figures and image-only card matches B,H,K require original teacher review; no publisher diagram pixels are reproduced.</p><h2>Activity 2 — Makes Sense to Me</h2><p>Create a group poster showing an assigned problem, equation, tape-bar reasoning and reasonableness check. Visit another poster and comment on the mathematical argument. Teacher assesses the discussion and collaboration.</p><p><a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-3/lesson-18/lesson.html">Original 2021 teacher lesson</a>. The gated original Cool-down is not included.</p></section>